{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1394785-mastering-purviews-in-2nd-edition","id":1394785,"title":"\"Mastering\" Purviews in 2nd Edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-07T08:56:38-07:00","id":1394785,"title":"\"Mastering\" Purviews in 2nd Edition?","content":"Something that's been bothering me since I got my hands on second edition, is how inherent purviews are handled. To start with, all Scions have 1 free purview that they can wield without the aid of any special relics or birthrights. But any other purviews need some kind of item or servant to help channel them.<br /> <br /> Unless that purview has been &quot;mastered&quot; if I understand correctly.<br /> <br /> So it seems like there is a way to obtain more than one inherent purview over the course of the game. But I have not personally been able to find details at the time of writing this.<br /> <br /> So I was hoping somebody else around here might be able to clarify it for me, seeing as how the Gods (to the best of my knowledge) don't need to rely on special artifacts and outside help to wield all the purviews at their disposal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26211-newnyrufa","name":"NewNyrufa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T09:54:50-07:00","id":1394792,"title":"","content":"In 1E, you have access to no purviews, only Epic Attributes, so it\u2019s basically the same thing, but on 2e you can also gain the purview from Guides, that are not there to use.<br /> <br /> I guess Demigods (or only Gods) can Master it and gain access to purviews with no birthright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider